{"jobs":[{"id":"199fd788-1f1a-4cec-8116-103d3c04a692","title":"Revenue Operations Manager","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-03T18:46:09.066+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/builder-prime/199fd788-1f1a-4cec-8116-103d3c04a692","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/builder-prime/199fd788-1f1a-4cec-8116-103d3c04a692/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>THE COMPANY</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Builder Prime, we’re revolutionizing the home improvement industry by doing more than just building software—we're giving hardworking contractors their time and freedom back. Our all-in-one business management solution is the essential platform for companies at their \"level-up\" moment, seamlessly integrating CRM, estimating, production management, payments, and reporting. By replacing disjointed tools with a unified data and automation foundation, we empower businesses to operate more efficiently, win more jobs, and achieve their growth goals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Builder Prime is backed by Blueprint Equity and is an AI-forward company. That means every employee is expected to use AI on real problems—not hypotheticals, not demos, but the actual work on their desk. We invest in tools, training, and time for our team to experiment and share what they learn. We’re not waiting on the sidelines, and we don’t have it all figured out. We’re building this practice alongside our team, in the open.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look for collaborative, community-oriented team members who bring initiative, curiosity, and a genuine interest in figuring out how AI can make their work and their customers’ outcomes better.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>THE ROLE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Builder Prime is a growing, Series B company where the RevOps function is at an inflection point. Our systems and processes are built out, but as the company scales, much of that infrastructure needs to be rearchitected to support the next stage of growth. This is a chance to take what exists, identify what needs to change, and rebuild it the right way. If you want to shape how a GTM org operates, not just maintain what someone else built, this role was designed for you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Revenue Operations Manager, you will own day-to-day operations across Sales, Marketing, and Customer Success. You will report to the Director of Revenue Operations and work directly with GTM leadership as a strategic partner. That means you will be in the room for planning conversations, your analysis will inform real decisions, and you will have the latitude to drive change across systems, processes, and tooling. RevOps at Builder Prime is a strategic function with a seat at the table, and this role carries real ownership and real influence.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is also a role at the front of a major shift. AI is changing what a lean RevOps team can accomplish, and we want someone who sees that as an opportunity to raise the ceiling on their own impact. You will have the tools and the freedom to rethink how reporting, enrichment, and automation get done, and to build workflows that punch well above their weight.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>This is a remote position open to candidates authorized to work in the US without visa sponsorship, who presently reside in the US. There is a preference for candidates in states where we already have Builder Prime employees: California, Colorado, Florida, Georgia, Idaho, Indiana, Nebraska, New York, Ohio, Oregon, Texas, Utah, Virginia, Washington, and Wisconsin. Builder Prime has an office in the greater Denver metro area (Westminster) that some of the sales team works out of.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>THE DAY-TO-DAY</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive Data-Driven Decision Making</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain the GTM source of truth: pipeline coverage, conversion rates, churn and retention, and activity pacing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop dashboards that GTM leaders actually use, not just ones that exist.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the narrative behind the numbers. Surface trends and risks proactively, without being asked.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the Revenue Infrastructure</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own HubSpot end to end: architecture, workflows, data integrity, and user governance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design a data model that stays trustworthy as volume grows, including the field standards, enrichment logic, and dedupe rules that hold up at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and automate cross-object associations, lead routing, deal desk workflows, and renewal and expansion triggers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish and protect CRM governance standards. RevOps owns the system; you are the last line of defense against configuration drift.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the operational handoff points across the funnel, from MQL to SAL to closed-won to onboarding. Ensure clean transitions, accurate stage definitions, and consistent data capture at every step so nothing falls through the cracks as deals move between teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>A note on the shape of this work: much of the current infrastructure needs to be rearchitected, not just maintained. The first two quarters will be front-loaded with a design phase that will include cleanup, normalization, and governance work. That foundation work is the highest-leverage thing you will do all year, because once it is right, everything downstream gets easier and your time shifts toward strategic analysis, optimization, and proactive insight. You are not inheriting someone else's system. You are redesigning it.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner Across the GTM Org</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the weekly and monthly GTM performance story end to end. You decide what the numbers are actually saying, what is working, what is not, and what needs to change, and you present that directly to GTM leadership. When the Director sets departmental strategy, she is building on your analysis. You are the person who turns raw funnel data into the point of view the leadership team makes decisions on.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with SDR and AE teams on pipeline governance, list building, sequence reporting, and activity tracking. Build scalable processes for territory and lead routing as the team grows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively flag conversion gaps and pipeline health issues before they become leadership problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own renewal and expansion dashboards. Track health scores, churn risk, and expansion signals with enough lead time for CX to act on them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with CX leadership to improve visibility into adoption, retention trends, and expansion forecasting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support Marketing on campaign setup, attribution modeling, and multi-channel performance reporting. Ensure inbound and outbound attribution is accurate, documented, and trusted by the team.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Evaluate and Optimize the GTM Stack</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Audit and optimize the GTM stack (HubSpot, Apollo, Clay, Gong, Claude, and others).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own vendor relationships, subscription management, and renewal decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate new tools with a bias toward outcomes, not features. Make the build-vs-buy call and own the rollout.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What Success Looks Like</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In your first year, success means the GTM org trusts the data, leadership uses your dashboards without asking for ad hoc pulls, and the systems you own run without daily intervention. You have rebuilt the parts of the infrastructure that needed it, established governance standards the team respects, and shifted from reactive firefighting to proactive analysis. Your manager is not reviewing your work line by line. You are bringing finished recommendations and she is saying yes, adjusting, or redirecting.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>HOW YOU WILL USE AI</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI is transforming what a small RevOps team can accomplish, and this role sits at the center of that shift. You will use AI tools daily to expand your reach, eliminate manual work, and operate at a level of output that would not have been possible two years ago. Here is what that looks like in practice:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI-assisted workflows to automate recurring reporting (pipeline coverage, churn risk, activity pacing) and eliminate manual data pulls across HubSpot, Gong, and other GTM tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI to accelerate prospecting and account research, surfacing high-fit targets and enriching account data to support both outbound and expansion motions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI to identify expansion-ready accounts by surfacing behavioral and firmographic signals, feeding a prioritized list into CX and AE workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate and implement new AI-powered tooling across the GTM stack, owning the build-vs-buy recommendation and rollout from end to end.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2><strong>THE MUST-HAVES</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5 years in RevOps, Sales Ops, or a cross-functional GTM Ops role at a high-growth SaaS company, with broad ownership across systems, processes, and analytics. At least 1 year must have been in a Revenue Operations Manager or equivalent title with full-cycle ownership of a CRM instance and GTM reporting stack. This is not an entry-level ops role. In exchange, you get real ownership, direct access to GTM leadership, and the autonomy to make decisions that shape how the company operates.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep HubSpot proficiency. You have owned an instance end to end, not just worked inside one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience rebuilding or rearchitecting GTM infrastructure to support a scaling org.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical instincts with the ability to move from data to insight to recommendation independently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success partnering cross-functionally with Sales, Marketing, and CX leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with attribution modeling and marketing automation platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practical AI literacy. You have used AI tools to solve real problems in your work and can speak to where it creates value versus noise. You can walk us through a specific workflow where you used AI to produce an outcome that would have taken significantly longer or been impossible without it. We will ask.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High ownership and comfort with ambiguity. You set your own agenda, flag problems early, and close the loop without being asked.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You default to bringing a recommendation, not a question. When given an outcome and context, you independently determine the approach, execute it, and bring the finished work for review. You do not need to co-build with your manager to produce quality output, and you flag problems early with a proposed solution attached.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>THE NICE-TO-HAVES</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a SaaS company serving SMB or contractor markets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">HubSpot Certifications: Marketing Hub, Sales Hub, Service Hub, Operations Hub, and/or HubSpot Reporting are a plus. <em>Experience is always more important than certifications.</em></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Clay, Apollo, Gong, Aircall, Claude, Zapier, Zendesk, CS Platforms (like Planhat or Gainsight), and/or Pendo.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to CPQ, billing systems, or revenue recognition workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting or building an outbound motion from scratch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with BI platforms and advanced analytics.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>THE BENEFITS</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why You'll Love Working Here:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional Health Coverage</strong> – We cover 95% of medical, dental, and vision premiums for employees (Aetna &amp; Guardian), plus 50% for dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Retirement Match</strong> – 401k with up to 4% company match that's immediately vested (no waiting period!)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Generous Time Off</strong> – 20 PTO days, 48 hours sick time, 9 paid holidays, plus a paid volunteer day to give back to your community</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Annual International Retreat</strong> – All-expenses-paid company trip to connect with teammates in amazing destinations (This year we went to Cancun, Mexico! Join us for our next one in 2027)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Life Happens Coverage</strong> – Company-paid life insurance ($50k), AD&amp;D, and short-term disability, plus optional accident, hospital, critical illness, and additional life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow With Us</strong> – $300 annual professional development stipend, plus an incredible sabbatical at 5 years (2 extra weeks PTO + $1,000 travel bonus)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comprehensive Parental Leave</strong> – 10 weeks paid parental leave for birthing parents, 4 weeks for non-birthing parents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Equipped From Day One</strong> – Company-provided laptop and all the equipment you need to succeed</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>PLUS…</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>Room to Grow</u>: We LOVE to promote from within. Show us your best stuff, and you’ll have ample opportunity to grow and advance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>Flexible Work Arrangements</u>: We are currently a mix of hybrid and fully remote roles across multiple time zones to support work-life balance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>We Hate Red Tape</u>: We never restrict our team’s creativity, so you’ll have the freedom to experiment and test out new ideas. At Builder Prime, <em>“Iterate To Innovate”</em> is a foundational philosophy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>Strong Culture</u>: Through the use of platforms like Bonusly, the Coffee Chat slack app, and other events and initiatives (both virtual and in-person), we strive to make work both a place where you can do the best work of your career AND have fun. There is no reason it can't be both!</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This position will pay a base salary of $125,000-$135,000 depending on experience and location, with an additional variable compensation element to be discussed in the interview process.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Builder Prime is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diversity at all levels. We also participate in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the U.S.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"THE COMPANY\n\nAt Builder Prime, we’re revolutionizing the home improvement industry by doing more than just building software—we're giving hardworking contractors their time and freedom back. Our all-in-one business management solution is the essential platform for companies at their \"level-up\" moment, seamlessly integrating CRM, estimating, production management, payments, and reporting. By replacing disjointed tools with a unified data and automation foundation, we empower businesses to operate more efficiently, win more jobs, and achieve their growth goals.\n\n\n\nBuilder Prime is backed by Blueprint Equity and is an AI-forward company. That means every employee is expected to use AI on real problems—not hypotheticals, not demos, but the actual work on their desk. We invest in tools, training, and time for our team to experiment and share what they learn. We’re not waiting on the sidelines, and we don’t have it all figured out. We’re building this practice alongside our team, in the open.\n\n\n\nWe look for collaborative, community-oriented team members who bring initiative, curiosity, and a genuine interest in figuring out how AI can make their work and their customers’ outcomes better.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nBuilder Prime is a growing, Series B company where the RevOps function is at an inflection point. Our systems and processes are built out, but as the company scales, much of that infrastructure needs to be rearchitected to support the next stage of growth. This is a chance to take what exists, identify what needs to change, and rebuild it the right way. If you want to shape how a GTM org operates, not just maintain what someone else built, this role was designed for you.\n\n\n\nAs the Revenue Operations Manager, you will own day-to-day operations across Sales, Marketing, and Customer Success. You will report to the Director of Revenue Operations and work directly with GTM leadership as a strategic partner. That means you will be in the room for planning conversations, your analysis will inform real decisions, and you will have the latitude to drive change across systems, processes, and tooling. RevOps at Builder Prime is a strategic function with a seat at the table, and this role carries real ownership and real influence.\n\n\n\nThis is also a role at the front of a major shift. AI is changing what a lean RevOps team can accomplish, and we want someone who sees that as an opportunity to raise the ceiling on their own impact. You will have the tools and the freedom to rethink how reporting, enrichment, and automation get done, and to build workflows that punch well above their weight.\n\n\n\nThis is a remote position open to candidates authorized to work in the US without visa sponsorship, who presently reside in the US. There is a preference for candidates in states where we already have Builder Prime employees: California, Colorado, Florida, Georgia, Idaho, Indiana, Nebraska, New York, Ohio, Oregon, Texas, Utah, Virginia, Washington, and Wisconsin. Builder Prime has an office in the greater Denver metro area (Westminster) that some of the sales team works out of.\n\n\n\n\nTHE DAY-TO-DAY\n\nDrive Data-Driven Decision Making\n\n - Build and maintain the GTM source of truth: pipeline coverage, conversion rates, churn and retention, and activity pacing.\n\n - Develop dashboards that GTM leaders actually use, not just ones that exist.\n\n - Own the narrative behind the numbers. Surface trends and risks proactively, without being asked.\n   \n   \n\nOwn the Revenue Infrastructure\n\n - Own HubSpot end to end: architecture, workflows, data integrity, and user governance.\n\n - Design a data model that stays trustworthy as volume grows, including the field standards, enrichment logic, and dedupe rules that hold up at scale.\n\n - Design and automate cross-object associations, lead routing, deal desk workflows, and renewal and expansion triggers.\n\n - Establish and protect CRM governance standards. RevOps owns the system; you are the last line of defense against configuration drift.\n\n - Own the operational handoff points across the funnel, from MQL to SAL to closed-won to onboarding. Ensure clean transitions, accurate stage definitions, and consistent data capture at every step so nothing falls through the cracks as deals move between teams.\n\nA note on the shape of this work: much of the current infrastructure needs to be rearchitected, not just maintained. The first two quarters will be front-loaded with a design phase that will include cleanup, normalization, and governance work. That foundation work is the highest-leverage thing you will do all year, because once it is right, everything downstream gets easier and your time shifts toward strategic analysis, optimization, and proactive insight. You are not inheriting someone else's system. You are redesigning it.\n\n\n\nPartner Across the GTM Org\n\n - Own the weekly and monthly GTM performance story end to end. You decide what the numbers are actually saying, what is working, what is not, and what needs to change, and you present that directly to GTM leadership. When the Director sets departmental strategy, she is building on your analysis. You are the person who turns raw funnel data into the point of view the leadership team makes decisions on.\n\n - Work with SDR and AE teams on pipeline governance, list building, sequence reporting, and activity tracking. Build scalable processes for territory and lead routing as the team grows.\n\n - Proactively flag conversion gaps and pipeline health issues before they become leadership problems.\n\n - Own renewal and expansion dashboards. Track health scores, churn risk, and expansion signals with enough lead time for CX to act on them.\n\n - Partner with CX leadership to improve visibility into adoption, retention trends, and expansion forecasting.\n\n - Support Marketing on campaign setup, attribution modeling, and multi-channel performance reporting. Ensure inbound and outbound attribution is accurate, documented, and trusted by the team.\n\n\n\nEvaluate and Optimize the GTM Stack\n\n - Audit and optimize the GTM stack (HubSpot, Apollo, Clay, Gong, Claude, and others).\n\n - Own vendor relationships, subscription management, and renewal decisions.\n\n - Evaluate new tools with a bias toward outcomes, not features. Make the build-vs-buy call and own the rollout.\n\n\n\nWhat Success Looks Like\n\nIn your first year, success means the GTM org trusts the data, leadership uses your dashboards without asking for ad hoc pulls, and the systems you own run without daily intervention. You have rebuilt the parts of the infrastructure that needed it, established governance standards the team respects, and shifted from reactive firefighting to proactive analysis. Your manager is not reviewing your work line by line. You are bringing finished recommendations and she is saying yes, adjusting, or redirecting.\n\n\n\n\nHOW YOU WILL USE AI\n\nAI is transforming what a small RevOps team can accomplish, and this role sits at the center of that shift. You will use AI tools daily to expand your reach, eliminate manual work, and operate at a level of output that would not have been possible two years ago. Here is what that looks like in practice:\n\n - Use AI-assisted workflows to automate recurring reporting (pipeline coverage, churn risk, activity pacing) and eliminate manual data pulls across HubSpot, Gong, and other GTM tools.\n\n - Use AI to accelerate prospecting and account research, surfacing high-fit targets and enriching account data to support both outbound and expansion motions.\n\n - Use AI to identify expansion-ready accounts by surfacing behavioral and firmographic signals, feeding a prioritized list into CX and AE workflows.\n\n - Evaluate and implement new AI-powered tooling across the GTM stack, owning the build-vs-buy recommendation and rollout from end to end.\n\n \n\n\nTHE MUST-HAVES\n\n - 3-5 years in RevOps, Sales Ops, or a cross-functional GTM Ops role at a high-growth SaaS company, with broad ownership across systems, processes, and analytics. At least 1 year must have been in a Revenue Operations Manager or equivalent title with full-cycle ownership of a CRM instance and GTM reporting stack. This is not an entry-level ops role. In exchange, you get real ownership, direct access to GTM leadership, and the autonomy to make decisions that shape how the company operates.\n\n - Deep HubSpot proficiency. You have owned an instance end to end, not just worked inside one.\n\n - Experience rebuilding or rearchitecting GTM infrastructure to support a scaling org.\n\n - Strong analytical instincts with the ability to move from data to insight to recommendation independently.\n\n - Demonstrated success partnering cross-functionally with Sales, Marketing, and CX leadership.\n\n - Experience with attribution modeling and marketing automation platforms.\n\n - Practical AI literacy. You have used AI tools to solve real problems in your work and can speak to where it creates value versus noise. You can walk us through a specific workflow where you used AI to produce an outcome that would have taken significantly longer or been impossible without it. We will ask.\n\n - High ownership and comfort with ambiguity. You set your own agenda, flag problems early, and close the loop without being asked.\n\n - You default to bringing a recommendation, not a question. When given an outcome and context, you independently determine the approach, execute it, and bring the finished work for review. You do not need to co-build with your manager to produce quality output, and you flag problems early with a proposed solution attached.\n\n\n\n\nTHE NICE-TO-HAVES\n\n - Experience in a SaaS company serving SMB or contractor markets.\n\n - HubSpot Certifications: Marketing Hub, Sales Hub, Service Hub, Operations Hub, and/or HubSpot Reporting are a plus. Experience is always more important than certifications.\n\n - Familiarity with Clay, Apollo, Gong, Aircall, Claude, Zapier, Zendesk, CS Platforms (like Planhat or Gainsight), and/or Pendo.\n\n - Exposure to CPQ, billing systems, or revenue recognition workflows.\n\n - Experience supporting or building an outbound motion from scratch.\n\n - Experience with BI platforms and advanced analytics.\n\n\n\n\nTHE BENEFITS\n\nWhy You'll Love Working Here:\n\n - Exceptional Health Coverage – We cover 95% of medical, dental, and vision premiums for employees (Aetna & Guardian), plus 50% for dependents\n\n - Strong Retirement Match – 401k with up to 4% company match that's immediately vested (no waiting period!)\n\n - Generous Time Off – 20 PTO days, 48 hours sick time, 9 paid holidays, plus a paid volunteer day to give back to your community\n\n - Annual International Retreat – All-expenses-paid company trip to connect with teammates in amazing destinations (This year we went to Cancun, Mexico! Join us for our next one in 2027)\n\n - Life Happens Coverage – Company-paid life insurance ($50k), AD&D, and short-term disability, plus optional accident, hospital, critical illness, and additional life insurance\n\n - Grow With Us – $300 annual professional development stipend, plus an incredible sabbatical at 5 years (2 extra weeks PTO + $1,000 travel bonus)\n\n - Comprehensive Parental Leave – 10 weeks paid parental leave for birthing parents, 4 weeks for non-birthing parents\n\n - Fully Equipped From Day One – Company-provided laptop and all the equipment you need to succeed\n\n\n\n\nPLUS…\n\n - Room to Grow: We LOVE to promote from within. Show us your best stuff, and you’ll have ample opportunity to grow and advance.\n\n - Flexible Work Arrangements: We are currently a mix of hybrid and fully remote roles across multiple time zones to support work-life balance.\n\n - We Hate Red Tape: We never restrict our team’s creativity, so you’ll have the freedom to experiment and test out new ideas. At Builder Prime, “Iterate To Innovate” is a foundational philosophy.\n\n - Strong Culture: Through the use of platforms like Bonusly, the Coffee Chat slack app, and other events and initiatives (both virtual and in-person), we strive to make work both a place where you can do the best work of your career AND have fun. There is no reason it can't be both!\n\n\n\nThis position will pay a base salary of $125,000-$135,000 depending on experience and location, with an additional variable compensation element to be discussed in the interview process.\n\nBuilder Prime is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diversity at all levels. We also participate in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the U.S.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$125K – $135K • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$125K - $135K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"9460b50c-6138-41ef-a5c4-b67f3481056e","tierSummary":"$125K – $135K • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6a797efa-6c75-4d94-b04d-39ce82a64694","summary":"$125K – $135K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":125000,"maxValue":135000},{"id":"ba29fe5d-f8b2-43ad-a524-7afddb917e64","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":125000,"maxValue":135000},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"50dd8569-5eaf-46a2-bdc7-c1508ed0c1ab","title":"Senior Demand Generation & Growth Marketing Manager","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-05T21:18:05.328+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/builder-prime/50dd8569-5eaf-46a2-bdc7-c1508ed0c1ab","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/builder-prime/50dd8569-5eaf-46a2-bdc7-c1508ed0c1ab/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>THE COMPANY</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Builder Prime, we're revolutionizing the home improvement industry by doing more than just building software—we're giving hardworking contractors their time and freedom back. Our all-in-one business management solution is the essential platform for companies at their \"level-up\" moment, seamlessly integrating CRM, estimating, production management, payments, and reporting. By replacing disjointed tools with a unified data and automation foundation, we empower businesses to operate more efficiently, win more jobs, and achieve their growth goals. We look for collaborative and community-oriented team members who bring initiative and curiosity to the challenge of solving problems for our customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Builder Prime is backed by Blueprint Equity and is an AI-forward company. That means every employee is expected to use AI on real problems—not hypotheticals, not demos, but the actual work on their desk. We invest in tools, training, and time for our team to experiment and share what they learn. We're not waiting on the sidelines, and we don't have it all figured out. We're building this practice alongside our team, in the open.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>THE ROLE</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This is a remote position open to candidates authorized to work in the US without visa sponsorship, who presently reside in the US.</strong><em> There is a preference for candidates in states where we already have Builder Prime employees; California, Colorado, Florida, Georgia, Idaho, Indiana, Nebraska, New York, Ohio, Oregon, Texas, Utah, Virginia, Washington, and Wisconsin. Builder Prime has an office in the greater Denver metro area (Westminster) that some of the sales team works out of.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are seeking a Senior Manager of Demand Generation and Growth Marketing to help manage and grow Builder Prime's demand engine. This is a hands-on individual contributor role that blends planning and execution. You will carry a sourced-pipeline number, diversify how we generate demand, sharpen the path from lead to closed deal, and pull our lead mix upmarket toward the customers we most want to win. You will set and run the day-to-day plan and work closely with our agency and operations partners on execution, in partnership with marketing leadership on strategy. The role starts with a demand generation mandate and has room to grow into broader, full-funnel growth as the function matures. This role reports to the SVP of Marketing.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>THE DAY-TO-DAY</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Demand Engine and Pipeline: </strong>Manage the demand generation plan and contribute to the sourced-pipeline number that feeds sales. Recommend the channel mix and budget allocation, and run the day-to-day of the engine, measured on pipeline, cost per lead, cost per MQL, channels launched and optimized, and campaign throughput. You set and manage the plan while marketing leadership holds overall strategy and final spend approval.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Paid Channels and Optimization: </strong>Diversify demand beyond paid search into new channels including LinkedIn, paid social, TikTok, retargeting, bumper video, and intent and review platforms such as Gartner and G2, then optimize relentlessly for efficiency and pipeline contribution. Work closely with our paid media agency partner, briefing campaigns and managing performance, while the hands-on campaign setup and trafficking run through the partner.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lead-to-Sale Orchestration: </strong>Own and fix the flow from lead to sale and the handoff to sales, cut by audience across SMB, mid-market, and enterprise, and by product interest. Partner closely with the SDR and sales teams on follow-up cadence and service-level agreements to ensure no qualified lead falls through the cracks, and serve as the connective tissue that keeps demand generation, operations, and sales aligned.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>ABX and ICP Targeting: </strong>Support and help grow an account-based (ABX) motion against our target-account list, and shift our lead mix upmarket toward ideal-customer-profile accounts and away from poor-fit, sub-scale leads. You contribute to the targeting logic and account selection, meaning who we go after and why, while marketing operations owns the hands-on list building, sequencing, and technical execution. Strategy and targeting live here; the build stays with ops.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>THE MUST-HAVES</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in demand generation or growth marketing, preferably at a high-growth B2B SaaS company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of owning a pipeline or MQL/SAL/SQL number and hitting it, with a goal- and KPI-driven, ROI-focused mindset.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience planning and managing paid media channels (paid search, LinkedIn, paid social, retargeting, video, and intent platforms such as Gartner &amp; G2) and directing agencies or vendors against a budget.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with account-based marketing or ABX, including how to define target accounts and coordinate air cover with sales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong command of marketing funnel and pipeline metrics (MQL, SQL, conversion rates, cost per lead, and cost per MQL), and comfort using attribution to prove sourced pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Can build and interpret dashboards and reporting for demand and growth channels, and knows reporting best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with CRM and marketing automation platforms such as HubSpot, and a clear understanding of how leads route, score, and flow to sales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to align cross-functional partners across marketing, operations, and sales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills with attention to detail, can prioritize a dynamic workload, and successfully handle multiple deadlines with a busy schedule.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, rapidly changing environment - move quickly, think strategically, identify opportunities, and excel at tactical execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adept at using Google Suite, Slack, and CRM software.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Self-starter. You can work on multiple projects with many stakeholders simultaneously. You take ownership, sweat the details, and see projects through to the end with little to no support needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness and ability to travel occasionally for company events, trade shows, and team offsites.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable using AI tools (such as Claude, ChatGPT, or similar) as part of your day-to-day work — not just for occasional tasks, but as a regular part of how you get things done.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to apply good judgment about when AI output should be reviewed, refined, or set aside. You understand that AI accelerates work; humans own the outcome.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curious about how AI could reshape your role and willing to experiment, share what you learn, and contribute to how we build these practices as a company.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>THE NICE-TO-HAVES</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge or experience in SaaS and the home improvement industry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience generating demand into mid-market and enterprise segments, or moving a lead mix upmarket.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with ABX or ABM platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A working understanding of outbound and data-enrichment tools such as Apollo, Clay, and Instantly, and the ability to bring strong use cases to the team that runs them, even if the hands-on build stays with operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A test-and-learn mindset, with experience running structured experiments to improve funnel conversion and channel efficiency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of business management CRM software and its application in improving business processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building or refining AI workflows, prompts, or automations in a professional context.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Early-stage start-up (series A/B) experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>THE BENEFITS</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why You'll Love Working Here:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional Health Coverage</strong> – We cover 95% of medical, dental, and vision premiums for employees (Aetna &amp; Guardian), plus 50% for dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Retirement Match</strong> – 401k with up to 4% company match that's immediately vested (no waiting period!)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Generous Time Off</strong> – 20 PTO days, 48 hours sick time, 9 paid holidays, plus a paid volunteer day to give back to your community</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Annual International Retreat</strong> – All-expenses-paid company trip to connect with teammates in amazing destinations (This year we went to Cancun, Mexico! Join us for our next one in 2027)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Life Happens Coverage</strong> – Company-paid life insurance ($50k), AD&amp;D, and short-term disability, plus optional accident, hospital, critical illness, and additional life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow With Us</strong> – $300 annual professional development stipend, plus an incredible sabbatical at 5 years (2 extra weeks PTO + $1,000 travel bonus)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comprehensive Parental Leave</strong> – 10 weeks paid parental leave for birthing parents, 4 weeks for non-birthing parents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Equipped From Day One</strong> – Company-provided laptop and all the equipment you need to succeed</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>PLUS…</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Room to Grow: </strong>We LOVE to promote from within. Show us your best stuff, and you'll have ample opportunity to grow and advance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flexible Work Arrangements: </strong>We are currently a mix of hybrid and fully remote roles across multiple time zones to support work-life balance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>We Hate Red Tape: </strong>We never restrict our team's creativity, so you'll have the freedom to experiment and test out new ideas. At Builder Prime, \"Iterate To Innovate\" is a foundational philosophy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Culture: </strong>Through the use of platforms like Bonusly, the Coffee Chat slack app, and other events and initiatives (both virtual and in-person), we strive to make work both a place where you can do the best work of your career AND have fun. There is no reason it can't be both!</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This position will pay a base salary of $135,000 to $145,000, depending on experience and location, with an additional variable compensation element to be discussed in the interview process.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Builder Prime is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diversity at all levels. We also participate in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the U.S.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"THE COMPANY\n\nAt Builder Prime, we're revolutionizing the home improvement industry by doing more than just building software—we're giving hardworking contractors their time and freedom back. Our all-in-one business management solution is the essential platform for companies at their \"level-up\" moment, seamlessly integrating CRM, estimating, production management, payments, and reporting. By replacing disjointed tools with a unified data and automation foundation, we empower businesses to operate more efficiently, win more jobs, and achieve their growth goals. We look for collaborative and community-oriented team members who bring initiative and curiosity to the challenge of solving problems for our customers.\n\nBuilder Prime is backed by Blueprint Equity and is an AI-forward company. That means every employee is expected to use AI on real problems—not hypotheticals, not demos, but the actual work on their desk. We invest in tools, training, and time for our team to experiment and share what they learn. We're not waiting on the sidelines, and we don't have it all figured out. We're building this practice alongside our team, in the open.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nThis is a remote position open to candidates authorized to work in the US without visa sponsorship, who presently reside in the US. There is a preference for candidates in states where we already have Builder Prime employees; California, Colorado, Florida, Georgia, Idaho, Indiana, Nebraska, New York, Ohio, Oregon, Texas, Utah, Virginia, Washington, and Wisconsin. Builder Prime has an office in the greater Denver metro area (Westminster) that some of the sales team works out of.\n\nWe are seeking a Senior Manager of Demand Generation and Growth Marketing to help manage and grow Builder Prime's demand engine. This is a hands-on individual contributor role that blends planning and execution. You will carry a sourced-pipeline number, diversify how we generate demand, sharpen the path from lead to closed deal, and pull our lead mix upmarket toward the customers we most want to win. You will set and run the day-to-day plan and work closely with our agency and operations partners on execution, in partnership with marketing leadership on strategy. The role starts with a demand generation mandate and has room to grow into broader, full-funnel growth as the function matures. This role reports to the SVP of Marketing.\n\n\n\nTHE DAY-TO-DAY\n\nDemand Engine and Pipeline: Manage the demand generation plan and contribute to the sourced-pipeline number that feeds sales. Recommend the channel mix and budget allocation, and run the day-to-day of the engine, measured on pipeline, cost per lead, cost per MQL, channels launched and optimized, and campaign throughput. You set and manage the plan while marketing leadership holds overall strategy and final spend approval.\n\nPaid Channels and Optimization: Diversify demand beyond paid search into new channels including LinkedIn, paid social, TikTok, retargeting, bumper video, and intent and review platforms such as Gartner and G2, then optimize relentlessly for efficiency and pipeline contribution. Work closely with our paid media agency partner, briefing campaigns and managing performance, while the hands-on campaign setup and trafficking run through the partner.\n\nLead-to-Sale Orchestration: Own and fix the flow from lead to sale and the handoff to sales, cut by audience across SMB, mid-market, and enterprise, and by product interest. Partner closely with the SDR and sales teams on follow-up cadence and service-level agreements to ensure no qualified lead falls through the cracks, and serve as the connective tissue that keeps demand generation, operations, and sales aligned.\n\nABX and ICP Targeting: Support and help grow an account-based (ABX) motion against our target-account list, and shift our lead mix upmarket toward ideal-customer-profile accounts and away from poor-fit, sub-scale leads. You contribute to the targeting logic and account selection, meaning who we go after and why, while marketing operations owns the hands-on list building, sequencing, and technical execution. Strategy and targeting live here; the build stays with ops.\n\n\n\n\nTHE MUST-HAVES\n\n - 5+ years of experience in demand generation or growth marketing, preferably at a high-growth B2B SaaS company.\n\n - A track record of owning a pipeline or MQL/SAL/SQL number and hitting it, with a goal- and KPI-driven, ROI-focused mindset.\n\n - Hands-on experience planning and managing paid media channels (paid search, LinkedIn, paid social, retargeting, video, and intent platforms such as Gartner & G2) and directing agencies or vendors against a budget.\n\n - Experience with account-based marketing or ABX, including how to define target accounts and coordinate air cover with sales.\n\n - Strong command of marketing funnel and pipeline metrics (MQL, SQL, conversion rates, cost per lead, and cost per MQL), and comfort using attribution to prove sourced pipeline.\n\n - Can build and interpret dashboards and reporting for demand and growth channels, and knows reporting best practices.\n\n - Familiarity with CRM and marketing automation platforms such as HubSpot, and a clear understanding of how leads route, score, and flow to sales.\n\n - Excellent communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to align cross-functional partners across marketing, operations, and sales.\n\n - Strong organizational skills with attention to detail, can prioritize a dynamic workload, and successfully handle multiple deadlines with a busy schedule.\n\n - Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, rapidly changing environment - move quickly, think strategically, identify opportunities, and excel at tactical execution.\n\n - Adept at using Google Suite, Slack, and CRM software.\n\n - Self-starter. You can work on multiple projects with many stakeholders simultaneously. You take ownership, sweat the details, and see projects through to the end with little to no support needed.\n\n - Willingness and ability to travel occasionally for company events, trade shows, and team offsites.\n\n - Comfortable using AI tools (such as Claude, ChatGPT, or similar) as part of your day-to-day work — not just for occasional tasks, but as a regular part of how you get things done.\n\n - Able to apply good judgment about when AI output should be reviewed, refined, or set aside. You understand that AI accelerates work; humans own the outcome.\n\n - Curious about how AI could reshape your role and willing to experiment, share what you learn, and contribute to how we build these practices as a company.\n\n\n\n\nTHE NICE-TO-HAVES\n\n - Knowledge or experience in SaaS and the home improvement industry.\n\n - Experience generating demand into mid-market and enterprise segments, or moving a lead mix upmarket.\n\n - Hands-on experience with ABX or ABM platforms.\n\n - A working understanding of outbound and data-enrichment tools such as Apollo, Clay, and Instantly, and the ability to bring strong use cases to the team that runs them, even if the hands-on build stays with operations.\n\n - A test-and-learn mindset, with experience running structured experiments to improve funnel conversion and channel efficiency.\n\n - Strong understanding of business management CRM software and its application in improving business processes.\n\n - Experience building or refining AI workflows, prompts, or automations in a professional context.\n\n - Early-stage start-up (series A/B) experience.\n\n\n\n\nTHE BENEFITS\n\nWhy You'll Love Working Here:\n\n - Exceptional Health Coverage – We cover 95% of medical, dental, and vision premiums for employees (Aetna & Guardian), plus 50% for dependents\n\n - Strong Retirement Match – 401k with up to 4% company match that's immediately vested (no waiting period!)\n\n - Generous Time Off – 20 PTO days, 48 hours sick time, 9 paid holidays, plus a paid volunteer day to give back to your community\n\n - Annual International Retreat – All-expenses-paid company trip to connect with teammates in amazing destinations (This year we went to Cancun, Mexico! Join us for our next one in 2027)\n\n - Life Happens Coverage – Company-paid life insurance ($50k), AD&D, and short-term disability, plus optional accident, hospital, critical illness, and additional life insurance\n\n - Grow With Us – $300 annual professional development stipend, plus an incredible sabbatical at 5 years (2 extra weeks PTO + $1,000 travel bonus)\n\n - Comprehensive Parental Leave – 10 weeks paid parental leave for birthing parents, 4 weeks for non-birthing parents\n\n - Fully Equipped From Day One – Company-provided laptop and all the equipment you need to succeed\n\n\n\nPLUS…\n\n - Room to Grow: We LOVE to promote from within. Show us your best stuff, and you'll have ample opportunity to grow and advance.\n\n - Flexible Work Arrangements: We are currently a mix of hybrid and fully remote roles across multiple time zones to support work-life balance.\n\n - We Hate Red Tape: We never restrict our team's creativity, so you'll have the freedom to experiment and test out new ideas. At Builder Prime, \"Iterate To Innovate\" is a foundational philosophy.\n\n - Strong Culture: Through the use of platforms like Bonusly, the Coffee Chat slack app, and other events and initiatives (both virtual and in-person), we strive to make work both a place where you can do the best work of your career AND have fun. There is no reason it can't be both!\n\n\n\nThis position will pay a base salary of $135,000 to $145,000, depending on experience and location, with an additional variable compensation element to be discussed in the interview process.\n\nBuilder Prime is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diversity at all levels. We also participate in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the U.S.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$135K – $145K • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$135K - $145K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ec3b18b8-60c4-4ffb-9f8d-16fbab399c60","tierSummary":"$135K – $145K • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"4585b4cd-c1f6-4be5-beac-0f53f5662fff","summary":"$135K – $145K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":135000,"maxValue":145000},{"id":"8f680b30-8bd9-4207-88a8-4c63889b34aa","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":135000,"maxValue":145000},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"57765345-61a0-4e66-b7ed-94c69cfff4fb","title":"Implementation Project Manager","department":"Customer Experience","team":"Customer Experience","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T21:32:11.746+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/builder-prime/57765345-61a0-4e66-b7ed-94c69cfff4fb","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/builder-prime/57765345-61a0-4e66-b7ed-94c69cfff4fb/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>THE COMPANY</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Builder Prime, we’re revolutionizing the home improvement industry by doing more than just building software—we're giving hardworking contractors their time and freedom back. Our all-in-one business management solution is the essential platform for companies at their \"level-up\" moment, seamlessly integrating CRM, estimating, production management, payments, and reporting. By replacing disjointed tools with a unified data and automation foundation, we empower businesses to operate more efficiently, win more jobs, and achieve their growth goals. We look for collaborative and community-oriented team members who bring initiative and curiosity to the challenge of solving problems for our customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Builder Prime is backed by Blueprint Equity and is an AI-forward company. That means every employee is expected to use AI on real problems—not hypotheticals, not demos, but the actual work on their desk. We invest in tools, training, and time for our team to experiment and share what they learn. We’re not waiting on the sidelines, and we don’t have it all figured out. We’re building this practice alongside our team, in the open.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look for collaborative, community-oriented team members who bring initiative, curiosity, and a genuine interest in figuring out how AI can make their work and their customers’ outcomes better.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>THE ROLE</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This is a remote position open to candidates authorized to work in the US without visa sponsorship, who presently reside in the US. </strong><em>There is a preference for candidates in states where we already have Builder Prime employees; California, Colorado, Florida, Georgia, Idaho, Indiana, Nebraska, New York, Ohio, Oregon, Texas, Utah, Virginia, Washington, and Wisconsin. Builder Prime has an office in the greater Denver metro area (Westminster) that some of the sales team works out of.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our implementation team facilitates smooth transitions for new customers by providing personalized implementation plans, technical configuration assistance, and comprehensive training to ensure effective software adoption and swift time to value.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a member of the implementation team, you will lead implementations and drive strategic improvements to our implementation methodology. You'll serve as the escalation point for challenging technical configurations and will be instrumental in reducing our overall customer onboarding timeline.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>THE DAY-TO-DAY</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Implementation Project Manager at Builder Prime, you are responsible for guiding new customers through the implementation process, ensuring they achieve rapid time-to-value from our platform. This role reports directly to the Manager of Implementation and collaborates closely with Account Managers, Support, and Sales.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive strategic initiatives to streamline implementation processes and reduce time-to-value</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage implementations with multiple stakeholders and complex technical requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead kickoff calls to understand customer goals, timeline expectations, and success metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Configure the platform with custom templates, workflows, and settings specific to each customer's needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare customers for post-implementation self-sufficiency by delivering system training as part of the Implementation process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track implementation milestones and manage customer expectations throughout the setup process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and solve technical challenges that arise during implementation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with Account Managers for a smooth handoff once implementation is complete</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document customer workflows and configurations for future reference and support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously optimize implementation processes to improve efficiency and customer satisfaction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze implementation data to identify bottlenecks and recommend process improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in cross-functional projects aimed at improving customer onboarding experience</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>THE MUST-HAVES</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience in customer onboarding, implementation, or training roles, preferably in SaaS or construction technology</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to translate technical product capabilities into business value for diverse customer workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of reducing implementation timelines and improving customer satisfaction scores</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with implementations involving multiple stakeholders and complex integrations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills with ability to use data to drive process improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience conducting engaging virtual training sessions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical configuration skills with the ability to learn and master new software platforms quickly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent project management abilities with a track record of meeting implementation deadlines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication skills, including the ability to adapt messaging to different learning styles</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>THE NICE-TO-HAVES</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge or experience in SaaS and the home improvement industry.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of business management CRM software and its application in improving business processes.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>THE BENEFITS</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why You'll Love Working Here:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional Health Coverage</strong> – We cover 95% of medical, dental, and vision premiums for employees (Aetna &amp; Guardian), plus 50% for dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Retirement Match</strong> – 401k with up to 4% company match that's immediately vested (no waiting period!)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Generous Time Off</strong> – 20 PTO days, 48 hours sick time, 9 paid holidays, plus a paid volunteer day to give back to your community</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Annual International Retreat</strong> – All-expenses-paid company trip to connect with teammates in amazing destinations (This year we went to Cancun, Mexico! Join us for our next one in 2027)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Life Happens Coverage</strong> – Company-paid life insurance ($50k), AD&amp;D, and short-term disability, plus optional accident, hospital, critical illness, and additional life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow With Us</strong> – $300 annual professional development stipend, plus an incredible sabbatical at 5 years (2 extra weeks PTO + $1,000 travel bonus)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comprehensive Parental Leave</strong> – 10 weeks paid parental leave for birthing parents, 4 weeks for non-birthing parents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Equipped From Day One</strong> – Company-provided laptop and all the equipment you need to succeed</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>PLUS…</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>Room to Grow</u>: We LOVE to promote from within. Show us your best stuff, and you’ll have ample opportunity to grow and advance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>Flexible Work Arrangements</u>: We are currently a mix of hybrid and fully remote roles across multiple time zones to support work-life balance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>We Hate Red Tape</u>: We never restrict our team’s creativity, so you’ll have the freedom to experiment and test out new ideas. At Builder Prime, <em>“Iterate To Innovate”</em> is a foundational philosophy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>Strong Culture</u>: Through the use of platforms like Bonusly, the Coffee Chat slack app, and other events and initiatives (both virtual and in-person), we strive to make work both a place where you can do the best work of your career AND have fun. There is no reason it can't be both!</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This position will pay a base salary of $65,000-$75,000 depending on experience and location.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Builder Prime is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diversity at all levels. We also participate in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the U.S.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"THE COMPANY\n\nAt Builder Prime, we’re revolutionizing the home improvement industry by doing more than just building software—we're giving hardworking contractors their time and freedom back. Our all-in-one business management solution is the essential platform for companies at their \"level-up\" moment, seamlessly integrating CRM, estimating, production management, payments, and reporting. By replacing disjointed tools with a unified data and automation foundation, we empower businesses to operate more efficiently, win more jobs, and achieve their growth goals. We look for collaborative and community-oriented team members who bring initiative and curiosity to the challenge of solving problems for our customers.\n\nBuilder Prime is backed by Blueprint Equity and is an AI-forward company. That means every employee is expected to use AI on real problems—not hypotheticals, not demos, but the actual work on their desk. We invest in tools, training, and time for our team to experiment and share what they learn. We’re not waiting on the sidelines, and we don’t have it all figured out. We’re building this practice alongside our team, in the open.\n\nWe look for collaborative, community-oriented team members who bring initiative, curiosity, and a genuine interest in figuring out how AI can make their work and their customers’ outcomes better.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nThis is a remote position open to candidates authorized to work in the US without visa sponsorship, who presently reside in the US. There is a preference for candidates in states where we already have Builder Prime employees; California, Colorado, Florida, Georgia, Idaho, Indiana, Nebraska, New York, Ohio, Oregon, Texas, Utah, Virginia, Washington, and Wisconsin. Builder Prime has an office in the greater Denver metro area (Westminster) that some of the sales team works out of.\n\nOur implementation team facilitates smooth transitions for new customers by providing personalized implementation plans, technical configuration assistance, and comprehensive training to ensure effective software adoption and swift time to value.\n\nAs a member of the implementation team, you will lead implementations and drive strategic improvements to our implementation methodology. You'll serve as the escalation point for challenging technical configurations and will be instrumental in reducing our overall customer onboarding timeline.\n\n \n\n\nTHE DAY-TO-DAY\n\nAs an Implementation Project Manager at Builder Prime, you are responsible for guiding new customers through the implementation process, ensuring they achieve rapid time-to-value from our platform. This role reports directly to the Manager of Implementation and collaborates closely with Account Managers, Support, and Sales.\n\n - Drive strategic initiatives to streamline implementation processes and reduce time-to-value\n\n - Manage implementations with multiple stakeholders and complex technical requirements\n\n - Lead kickoff calls to understand customer goals, timeline expectations, and success metrics\n\n - Configure the platform with custom templates, workflows, and settings specific to each customer's needs\n\n - Prepare customers for post-implementation self-sufficiency by delivering system training as part of the Implementation process.\n\n - Track implementation milestones and manage customer expectations throughout the setup process\n\n - Identify and solve technical challenges that arise during implementation\n\n - Coordinate with Account Managers for a smooth handoff once implementation is complete\n\n - Document customer workflows and configurations for future reference and support\n\n - Continuously optimize implementation processes to improve efficiency and customer satisfaction\n\n - Analyze implementation data to identify bottlenecks and recommend process improvements\n\n - Participate in cross-functional projects aimed at improving customer onboarding experience\n\n\n\n\nTHE MUST-HAVES\n\n - 3+ years of experience in customer onboarding, implementation, or training roles, preferably in SaaS or construction technology\n\n - Demonstrated ability to translate technical product capabilities into business value for diverse customer workflows\n\n - Proven track record of reducing implementation timelines and improving customer satisfaction scores\n\n - Experience with implementations involving multiple stakeholders and complex integrations\n\n - Strong analytical skills with ability to use data to drive process improvements\n\n - Experience conducting engaging virtual training sessions\n\n - Strong technical configuration skills with the ability to learn and master new software platforms quickly\n\n - Excellent project management abilities with a track record of meeting implementation deadlines\n\n - Exceptional communication skills, including the ability to adapt messaging to different learning styles\n   \n   \n\n\nTHE NICE-TO-HAVES\n\n - Knowledge or experience in SaaS and the home improvement industry.\n\n - Strong understanding of business management CRM software and its application in improving business processes.\n\n\n\n\nTHE BENEFITS\n\nWhy You'll Love Working Here:\n\n - Exceptional Health Coverage – We cover 95% of medical, dental, and vision premiums for employees (Aetna & Guardian), plus 50% for dependents\n\n - Strong Retirement Match – 401k with up to 4% company match that's immediately vested (no waiting period!)\n\n - Generous Time Off – 20 PTO days, 48 hours sick time, 9 paid holidays, plus a paid volunteer day to give back to your community\n\n - Annual International Retreat – All-expenses-paid company trip to connect with teammates in amazing destinations (This year we went to Cancun, Mexico! Join us for our next one in 2027)\n\n - Life Happens Coverage – Company-paid life insurance ($50k), AD&D, and short-term disability, plus optional accident, hospital, critical illness, and additional life insurance\n\n - Grow With Us – $300 annual professional development stipend, plus an incredible sabbatical at 5 years (2 extra weeks PTO + $1,000 travel bonus)\n\n - Comprehensive Parental Leave – 10 weeks paid parental leave for birthing parents, 4 weeks for non-birthing parents\n\n - Fully Equipped From Day One – Company-provided laptop and all the equipment you need to succeed\n   \n   \n\n\nPLUS…\n\n - Room to Grow: We LOVE to promote from within. Show us your best stuff, and you’ll have ample opportunity to grow and advance.\n\n - Flexible Work Arrangements: We are currently a mix of hybrid and fully remote roles across multiple time zones to support work-life balance.\n\n - We Hate Red Tape: We never restrict our team’s creativity, so you’ll have the freedom to experiment and test out new ideas. At Builder Prime, “Iterate To Innovate” is a foundational philosophy.\n\n - Strong Culture: Through the use of platforms like Bonusly, the Coffee Chat slack app, and other events and initiatives (both virtual and in-person), we strive to make work both a place where you can do the best work of your career AND have fun. There is no reason it can't be both!\n\n\n\nThis position will pay a base salary of $65,000-$75,000 depending on experience and location.\n\nBuilder Prime is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diversity at all levels. We also participate in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the U.S.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$65K – $75K","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$65K - $75K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"e49ee94b-15c0-4a0d-9816-2457eed19a50","tierSummary":"$65K – $75K","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f49a0a6c-d3ad-4550-ac2d-7281ab5a03b0","summary":"$65K – $75K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":65000,"maxValue":75000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":65000,"maxValue":75000}]}},{"id":"319ae148-e75a-4438-9def-e8e7def733a9","title":"Outbound Sales Development Representative ","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote - US ","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T03:12:11.250+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/builder-prime/319ae148-e75a-4438-9def-e8e7def733a9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/builder-prime/319ae148-e75a-4438-9def-e8e7def733a9/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1><strong>THE COMPANY</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Builder Prime, we’re revolutionizing the home improvement industry by doing more than just building software—we're giving hardworking contractors their time and freedom back. Our all-in-one business operating solution is the essential platform for companies at their \"level-up\" moment, seamlessly integrating CRM, estimating, production management, payments, and reporting. By replacing disjointed tools with a unified data and automation foundation, we empower businesses to operate more efficiently, win more jobs, and achieve their growth goals. We look for collaborative and community-oriented team members who bring initiative and curiosity to the challenge of solving problems for our customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Builder Prime is backed by Blueprint Equity and is an AI-forward company. That means every employee is expected to use AI on real problems—not hypotheticals, not demos, but the actual work on their desk. We invest in tools, training, and time for our team to experiment and share what they learn. We’re not waiting on the sidelines, and we don’t have it all figured out. We’re building this practice alongside our team, in the open.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We look for collaborative, community-oriented team members who bring initiative, curiosity, and a genuine interest in figuring out how AI can make their work and their customers’ outcomes better.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>THE ROLE</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This is a remote role open to candidates authorized to work in the US without visa sponsorship, with a strong preference for candidates based in the greater Denver, CO or Salt Lake City, UT areas. </strong>Denver-based team members have the option to work from our Westminster, CO office, but it's not required.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ready to launch your sales career with a fast-growing SaaS company? As an Outbound SDR at Builder Prime, you'll be at the forefront of our growth, connecting with construction professionals who need our innovative software solutions. This isn't just cold calling—it's about building relationships, solving real problems, and directly impacting our company's success.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h1><strong>THE DAY-TO-DAY</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hunt for opportunities </strong>– Engage in strategic outbound prospecting through calls, emails, and social channels to connect with potential customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Tell our story</strong> – Showcase Builder Prime's value proposition in ways that resonate with construction professionals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualify and connect </strong>– Identify prospect needs, provide tailored solutions, and schedule qualified demos with our Account Executives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own your pipeline </strong>– Build and maintain a healthy flow of prospects while collaborating with the sales team on follow-up strategies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Stay sharp </strong>– Become a product expert who can speak confidently about how we solve real problems for our customers, with access to developmental opportunities like sales book clubs and training programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive results </strong>– Track your activities and performance, reporting to the Senior Manager of Sales Development. Compete in friendly monthly challenges and celebrate your wins with the team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>CAREER GROWTH</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're invested in your career progression. Builder Prime has a structured growth framework with clear metrics that show what success looks like at each stage of your SDR career. You'll know what's expected, how you're tracking, and how your compensation grows as you build your skills. When a business need opens up for the next role, you'll be ready for it, and you'll know exactly what got you there. We'll share more details in the interview process!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>THE MUST-HAVES</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree OR 2+ years of professional experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Outstanding communication skills—you know how to listen, connect, and persuade</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Creative problem-solving abilities and analytical thinking</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine enthusiasm for technology and innovation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stellar organizational skills with an eye for detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hunger to learn, grow, and advance your sales career</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A competitive drive and the coachability to act on feedback quickly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of taking ownership and pushing through obstacles, whether in school, sports, past jobs, or other pursuits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable using AI tools (such as Claude, ChatGPT, or similar) as part of your day-to-day work — not just for occasional tasks, but as a regular part of how you get things done.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to apply good judgment about when AI output should be reviewed, refined, or set aside. You understand that AI accelerates work; humans own the outcome.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curious about how AI could reshape your role and willing to experiment, share what you learn, and contribute to how we build these practices as a company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable internet connection and a quiet, distraction-free space to work from home.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>THE NICE-TO-HAVES</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with HubSpot or similar CRM platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in SaaS or the construction industry</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of overachievement as a career SDR or AE (think President's Club, Rep of the Year, or similar recognition)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in a high effort, relationship driven field such as hospitality, logistics, or sales outside of SaaS, especially if you're looking to break into tech</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>THE BENEFITS</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why You'll Love Working Here:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional Health Coverage</strong> – We cover 95% of medical, dental, and vision premiums for employees (Aetna &amp; Guardian), plus 50% for dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Retirement Match</strong> – 401k with up to 4% company match that's immediately vested (no waiting period!)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Generous Time Off</strong> – 20 PTO days, 48 hours sick time, 9 paid holidays, plus a paid volunteer day to give back to your community</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Annual International Retreat</strong> – All-expenses-paid company trip to connect with teammates in amazing destinations (This year we went to Cancun, Mexico! Join us for our next one in 2027)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Life Happens Coverage</strong> – Company-paid life insurance ($50k), AD&amp;D, and short-term disability, plus optional accident, hospital, critical illness, and additional life insurance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Grow With Us</strong> – $300 annual professional development stipend, plus an incredible sabbatical at 5 years (2 extra weeks PTO + $1,000 travel bonus)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comprehensive Parental Leave</strong> – 10 weeks paid parental leave for birthing parents, 4 weeks for non-birthing parents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Fully Equipped From Day One</strong> – Company-provided laptop and all the equipment you need to succeed</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>PLUS…</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>Room to Grow</u>: We LOVE to promote from within. Show us your best stuff, and you’ll have ample opportunity to grow and advance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>We Hate Red Tape</u>: We never restrict our team’s creativity, so you’ll have the freedom to experiment and test out new ideas. At Builder Prime, <em>“Iterate To Innovate”</em> is a foundational philosophy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><u>Strong Culture</u>: Through the use of platforms like Bonusly, the Coffee Chat slack app, and other events and initiatives (both virtual and in-person), we strive to make work both a place where you can do the best work of your career AND have fun. There is no reason it can't be both!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This role pays a base salary of $60,000/year and a $20,000/year variable (monthly commissions are based on sales qualified lead (SQL) targets), for total On-Target Earnings (OTE) of $80,000.</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Builder Prime is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diversity at all levels. We also participate in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the U.S.</em></p>","descriptionPlain":"THE COMPANY\n\nAt Builder Prime, we’re revolutionizing the home improvement industry by doing more than just building software—we're giving hardworking contractors their time and freedom back. Our all-in-one business operating solution is the essential platform for companies at their \"level-up\" moment, seamlessly integrating CRM, estimating, production management, payments, and reporting. By replacing disjointed tools with a unified data and automation foundation, we empower businesses to operate more efficiently, win more jobs, and achieve their growth goals. We look for collaborative and community-oriented team members who bring initiative and curiosity to the challenge of solving problems for our customers.\n\nBuilder Prime is backed by Blueprint Equity and is an AI-forward company. That means every employee is expected to use AI on real problems—not hypotheticals, not demos, but the actual work on their desk. We invest in tools, training, and time for our team to experiment and share what they learn. We’re not waiting on the sidelines, and we don’t have it all figured out. We’re building this practice alongside our team, in the open.\n\nWe look for collaborative, community-oriented team members who bring initiative, curiosity, and a genuine interest in figuring out how AI can make their work and their customers’ outcomes better.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nThis is a remote role open to candidates authorized to work in the US without visa sponsorship, with a strong preference for candidates based in the greater Denver, CO or Salt Lake City, UT areas. Denver-based team members have the option to work from our Westminster, CO office, but it's not required.\n\nReady to launch your sales career with a fast-growing SaaS company? As an Outbound SDR at Builder Prime, you'll be at the forefront of our growth, connecting with construction professionals who need our innovative software solutions. This isn't just cold calling—it's about building relationships, solving real problems, and directly impacting our company's success.\n\n \n\n\nTHE DAY-TO-DAY\n\n - Hunt for opportunities – Engage in strategic outbound prospecting through calls, emails, and social channels to connect with potential customers\n\n - Tell our story – Showcase Builder Prime's value proposition in ways that resonate with construction professionals\n\n - Qualify and connect – Identify prospect needs, provide tailored solutions, and schedule qualified demos with our Account Executives\n\n - Own your pipeline – Build and maintain a healthy flow of prospects while collaborating with the sales team on follow-up strategies\n\n - Stay sharp – Become a product expert who can speak confidently about how we solve real problems for our customers, with access to developmental opportunities like sales book clubs and training programs\n\n - Drive results – Track your activities and performance, reporting to the Senior Manager of Sales Development. Compete in friendly monthly challenges and celebrate your wins with the team\n\n\n\n\nCAREER GROWTH\n\nWe're invested in your career progression. Builder Prime has a structured growth framework with clear metrics that show what success looks like at each stage of your SDR career. You'll know what's expected, how you're tracking, and how your compensation grows as you build your skills. When a business need opens up for the next role, you'll be ready for it, and you'll know exactly what got you there. We'll share more details in the interview process!\n\n\n\n\nTHE MUST-HAVES\n\n - Bachelor's degree OR 2+ years of professional experience\n\n - Outstanding communication skills—you know how to listen, connect, and persuade\n\n - Creative problem-solving abilities and analytical thinking\n\n - Genuine enthusiasm for technology and innovation\n\n - Stellar organizational skills with an eye for detail\n\n - Hunger to learn, grow, and advance your sales career\n\n - A competitive drive and the coachability to act on feedback quickly\n\n - A track record of taking ownership and pushing through obstacles, whether in school, sports, past jobs, or other pursuits\n\n - Comfortable using AI tools (such as Claude, ChatGPT, or similar) as part of your day-to-day work — not just for occasional tasks, but as a regular part of how you get things done.\n\n - Able to apply good judgment about when AI output should be reviewed, refined, or set aside. You understand that AI accelerates work; humans own the outcome.\n\n - Curious about how AI could reshape your role and willing to experiment, share what you learn, and contribute to how we build these practices as a company.\n\n - Reliable internet connection and a quiet, distraction-free space to work from home.\n\n\n\n\nTHE NICE-TO-HAVES\n\n - Experience with HubSpot or similar CRM platforms\n\n - Background in SaaS or the construction industry\n\n - A track record of overachievement as a career SDR or AE (think President's Club, Rep of the Year, or similar recognition)\n\n - Experience in a high effort, relationship driven field such as hospitality, logistics, or sales outside of SaaS, especially if you're looking to break into tech\n\n\n\n\nTHE BENEFITS\n\nWhy You'll Love Working Here:\n\n - Exceptional Health Coverage – We cover 95% of medical, dental, and vision premiums for employees (Aetna & Guardian), plus 50% for dependents\n\n - Strong Retirement Match – 401k with up to 4% company match that's immediately vested (no waiting period!)\n\n - Generous Time Off – 20 PTO days, 48 hours sick time, 9 paid holidays, plus a paid volunteer day to give back to your community\n\n - Annual International Retreat – All-expenses-paid company trip to connect with teammates in amazing destinations (This year we went to Cancun, Mexico! Join us for our next one in 2027)\n\n - Life Happens Coverage – Company-paid life insurance ($50k), AD&D, and short-term disability, plus optional accident, hospital, critical illness, and additional life insurance\n\n - Grow With Us – $300 annual professional development stipend, plus an incredible sabbatical at 5 years (2 extra weeks PTO + $1,000 travel bonus)\n\n - Comprehensive Parental Leave – 10 weeks paid parental leave for birthing parents, 4 weeks for non-birthing parents\n\n - Fully Equipped From Day One – Company-provided laptop and all the equipment you need to succeed\n\n\n\nPLUS…\n\n - Room to Grow: We LOVE to promote from within. Show us your best stuff, and you’ll have ample opportunity to grow and advance.\n\n - We Hate Red Tape: We never restrict our team’s creativity, so you’ll have the freedom to experiment and test out new ideas. At Builder Prime, “Iterate To Innovate” is a foundational philosophy.\n\n - Strong Culture: Through the use of platforms like Bonusly, the Coffee Chat slack app, and other events and initiatives (both virtual and in-person), we strive to make work both a place where you can do the best work of your career AND have fun. There is no reason it can't be both!\n   \n   \n\nThis role pays a base salary of $60,000/year and a $20,000/year variable (monthly commissions are based on sales qualified lead (SQL) targets), for total On-Target Earnings (OTE) of $80,000.\n\n\n\nBuilder Prime is an Equal Opportunity Employer and values diversity at all levels. We also participate in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the U.S.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$60K • $20K Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$60K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"9ce7ebce-f735-48f5-b9c5-4aedf30a6440","tierSummary":"$60K • $20K Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ea3ec6ae-786d-4466-9865-c747626cdfdb","summary":"$60K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":60000,"maxValue":60000},{"id":"dd79921a-9099-43c6-8d1b-ef30fa55cee4","summary":"$20K Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":20000,"maxValue":20000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":60000,"maxValue":60000},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":20000,"maxValue":20000}]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}